    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5848" root="جشر" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشِيرٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَشَرٌ</span> ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A</i> [<i>quiver of the kind
called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَفْضَة</span>; (S, K;) i. e., a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِنَانَة</span>; and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَفِيرٌ</span>;
accord. to ISd, <i>a</i> [<i>quiver of the kind called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَعْبَة</span>,
<i>of skins, slit in the side in order that the wind
may enter it and the feathers may therefore not
be eaten:</i> (TA:) or, accord. to Z, <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِرَابٌ</span>
(IAth, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>A large</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُوَالِق</span> [or <i>sack</i>]:
(S, K:) pl. [of pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْشِرَةٌ</span> and [of mult.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُشُرٌ</span>.
(TA.)

